# HELP lith_prefetch_unread_resident_bytes Bytes HELD IN THE MEMORY TIER that nothing has read. This -- not lith_prefetch_committed_bytes -- is the quantity eviction-before-read is about: committed counts from dispatch and so includes bytes still in flight, which cannot evict anything. Compare against --mem-cache, not --prefetch-budget: the collapse condition is this approaching tier CAPACITY, at which point every arriving chunk must evict an unread one (#313).
# TYPE lith_prefetch_unread_resident_bytes gauge
lith_prefetch_unread_resident_bytes 4.49839104e+08
# HELP lith_prefetch_used_total Prefetched chunks TOUCHED by a later demand read (same 1 MiB unit as lith_prefetch_issued_total). A CHUNK-TOUCH count, not a byte count: a 64 KiB read marks the whole 1 MiB chunk used, so used/issued OVERSTATES byte follow-through, and overstates it most for the scattered readers where prefetch is least useful. Measured case: 89% by this ratio against at most ~25% of the prefetched bytes actually read. Do not read it as a byte efficiency (#256).
# TYPE lith_prefetch_used_total counter
lith_prefetch_used_total 2419
